+"root_cause":"Layer note: the real layer is the Docket screen and shell (react-web 'screen'). The schema's layer list has no ui value, so 'api' stands in for the outermost layer. Symptom: the Plan nav entry opens a bulleted list headed 'Choose a plan'. It shows no tabs and loads no plan. The amended line (bug-002.dag.yaml:137) asks for 'a plan page with every plan in trace.json as a tab'. Cause: the green pointed the entry at a new route that is not a plan page. Frame.tsx:18 sets the entry's href to '#/plans'. u2Routes.tsx:9 sends that route to PlanIndex, and PlanIndex.tsx:12-23 draws a Rung region 'plan-index' with a <ul> of links. That region is in no signed-off screen under docs/ui/ (a grep for 'plan-index' and 'Choose a plan' finds nothing), so it breaks the react-web rule 'screens are composed, not designed'. The plan tabs never appear there because Frame.tsx:134 draws the 'Plans' Tabs only when planPage (useMatch('/plans/:planId'), Frame.tsx:80 area) matches, and '#/plans' does not match it. The green also added planIndex wiring for this page: Frame.tsx:80 useMatch('/plans'), :95 the title 'Plans', :116 the nav-current case. The comment at :129-130 says 'the Plan nav entry opens the list of them'. The same cause makes U2 dag-1.spec.ts:177 fail: that test expects the entry's href to be route.plan('build'). The amended line and main both agree with that test, so it is a correct regression signal, not a wrong expectation. Fix direction: give the Plan entry back main's target, which is a plan page where the existing Plans tab strip is drawn. Remove the PlanIndex screen, its '/plans' route and Frame's planIndex title, current and comment wiring. Keep the rest of the green (DATA-4, AGENT-2, HONEST-1, NotBuiltRegion).",
