+{"id":"I2","rule_id":"DAG-1","layer":"tests","files":["tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/e2e/N4/dag-1.spec.ts","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/unit/screens/dag-1-plan-nav-entry.test.tsx"],
+"root_cause":"Symptom: both N4 DAG-1 reproduction tests would fail against the behaviour David asked for. Cause: they encode the superseded inv-009 #11 I16 reading. That reading said 'offer every plan without landing on the build plan'. Steer D1 replaces it with 'land on a plan page that tabs every plan'. In e2e/N4/dag-1.spec.ts:21 the title says 'without landing on the build plan', and :31 asserts not.toHaveURL(/#\\/plans\\/build$/). In unit/screens/dag-1-plan-nav-entry.test.tsx:53 the title says the same, and :62 asserts window.location.hash is not '#/plans/build'. The header comments in both files (e2e :1-6, unit :1-5) give the 2026-10-23 'fix the nav' ruling as their authority, and D1 has since superseded it. The rest of each test is satisfied by main's tab strip: they find the entry, click it and expect all three '#/plans/<id>' links (e2e :28-30, unit :61). These two tests are what forced the green to build a page other than a plan page (I1). I1 and I2 share the same upstream cause, the superseded reading, but they are separate findings in separate layers. Fix direction: replace the 'never lands on build' assertions and titles with the amended behaviour. That behaviour is: the entry opens a plan page, every plan is a tab in the 'Plans' landmark, and clicking a tab loads that plan. Rewrite the header comments to cite steer D1. These are red-commit tests, and changing them is allowed only because David's steer D1 authorises it (loop.jsonl:6). The fix commit should say so, so the review does not read it as a test weakened after red.",
