+   "root_cause":"Symptom (e2e3 log lines 4784-4815): expected comps ['not-built-yet'] in the scope-note region, received []. The app does what N4's acceptance asks: Matrix.tsx:154-161 now fills Step 3 with ScopeNote (Matrix.tsx:92-103), a plain paragraph built from rules[].matrix with no kit component and no not-built-yet marker. The tests check it against a reference that predates the change. data-4.spec.ts:223-225 calls expectRegionComponents (parity.ts:105-115), which reads U1's own frozen reference through readReference (U1/support/reference.ts:16-18). In docs/ui/derived/U1/matrix/populated.html:44 that region still holds the kit-not-built-yet__box ('SELL-7 traited count has nothing to show yet'). The signed-off screen docs/ui/screens/matrix/populated.html:44, the source every derived reference is made from, holds the same box, and no docs/ui/derived/bug-002-N4/ exists. The in-transit escape cannot help: built.ts:76-77 regionSettled compares only whether a region is built, and U1 derived.json:38-44 and bug-002-N3 derived.json:73-79 both list this region as built. A placeholder component inside a built region is invisible to it. So the U1 assertion is stale against a design change David asked for ('build the note', inv-009 #8, I6), not a code defect. The N4 red step changed the behaviour without moving the screen contract and the reference the earlier node's parity reads. N2 hit the same pattern and solved it in W2/support/cancel.ts:258-267, by deriving its own reference and pointing W2's parity at it.",
