+  {"id":"I2","rule_id":"DATA-4","layer":"tests",
+   "files":["docs/ui/baselines/matrix/populated-1440-light.png","docs/ui/baselines/matrix/populated-390-light.png","docs/ui/baselines/matrix/populated-390-dark.png","docs/ui/baselines/matrix/populated-1440-dark.png","tests/Uinsure.Policies.Web.Tests/e2e/regression/matrix.spec.ts","src/Uinsure.Policies.Web/app/explorer/matrix/Matrix.tsx"],
+   "root_cause":"Same cause as I1, kept as a separate finding because it fails through the baselines rather than the reference. The matrix baselines in docs/ui/baselines/matrix/ were captured while Step 3 still drew the not-built-yet box. Matrix.tsx:160 now draws the ScopeNote paragraph, so the bottom of the page changes. That fits the log. 1440 light (log 841-880): same height, 5739 px (0.01) different, a change confined to one area. 390 light and 390 dark (log 1026-1048 and 1077-1099): 4370 px tall to 4362 px, 9275 and 13290 px (0.01) different; a box swapped for one paragraph shortens the page slightly. 1440 dark (log 977-988) did not compare at all: it timed out in page.waitForLoadState('networkidle') at regression/support/regression.ts:94. That is a load symptom, of the same kind as the loop long-content failure. This run cannot show that 1440 dark shares the cause, though it very likely will once it renders. The diffs are an intended change from N4's DATA-4 acceptance line, not a regression. Per web-testing they are a new baseline shown to David at Pause 2.",
